.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt WATTLE-APPLICATIONS 7
.Os Wattle DEVEL
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm wattle-applications
.Nd how Wattle applications are laid out and installed
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An application is a project that
.Xr wattle-apps 1
installs.
This page describes what an application contains beyond what
any project contains,
and where its files are installed.
The info file,
the exes,
libs and docs and the dependencies of a project are described
in
.Xr wattle-projects 7 ,
and
.Xr wattle-build 1
builds the exes and libs that an application declares.
.
.Sh LAYOUT
An application may contain these files:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql "info\&.edn"
.Xc
The info file,
at the root of the application.
Installing needs its
.Ql ":name"
and
.Ql ":group" .
See
.Ql "INFO FILE"
in
.Xr wattle-projects 7 .
.It Xo
.Ql "hooks/init\&.wattle"  or
.Ql "hooks\&.wattle"
.Xc
The application script.
If both exist,
.Ql "hooks/init\&.wattle"
is used.
The rest of
.Ql "hooks"
is installed with it,
so the script can import the files beside it.
.El
.Pp
An application needs an application script or an info file that
declares
.Ql ":exes" .
.
.Sh INSTALLATION
An application with an application script is installed by running
the hooks that the script defines,
and nothing else.
An application without one is installed from its info file.
Each exe of
.Ql ":type"
.Ql ":native"
or
.Ql ":source"
is installed,
with the libs and docs whose
.Ql ":for"
names it:
.Bl -bullet -offset 3n
.It
A
.Ql ":native"
exe is built with
.Xr wattle-build 1
and its program is installed in
.Ql "bin" .
A native lib for it is linked into the program,
and a source lib for it is compiled into the program.
.It
A
.Ql ":source"
exe is installed as described in
.Sx "Source programs" .
.It
Each file of a
.Ql ":man"
doc is installed in
.Ql "share/man" ,
in the section that the digit at the end of its name gives.
.El
.Pp
A
.Ql ":remote"
lib is fetched under
.Ql "lib/wattle/\&.fetch"
and has the form its own info file declares.
The manifest records the
.Ql ":name" ,
.Ql ":url"
and
.Ql ":rev"
of each under
.Ql ":libs" .
.Pp
A
.Ql ":web"
exe is not installed.
A lib or doc whose
.Ql ":for"
names no installed exe is not installed,
and a
.Ql ":web"
doc whose
.Ql ":for"
names an installed exe is refused.
The manifest lists each file installed in
.Ql "bin"
and
.Ql "share/man" ,
so
.Ql "wattle apps remove"
removes them with the application directory.
.
.Ss Source programs
A
.Ql ":source"
exe is a program that is installed as source.
Its
.Ql ":files"
are copied into the application directory.
A directory is copied without any entry named
.Ql "zig-out" ,
.Ql "\&.zig-cache" ,
.Ql "\&.wattle"
or
.Ql "\&.git" .
A source lib for it is copied to
.Ql "\&.wattle/<name>/"
there.
A native lib for it is built with
.Xr wattle-build 1
in the project,
and the native module is copied to
.Ql "zig-out/lib"
in the application directory.
This needs
.Ic zig
on the
.Ql "PATH" ,
and
.Ql "wattle apps upgrade"
builds the modules again.
.Pp
The program in
.Ql "bin"
has the name of the exe and starts with
.Ql "#!/usr/bin/env wattle" .
It loads
.Ql ":entry"
and calls
.Ql "main"
with the path of the program followed by the arguments.
A bare
.Ql "import"
in the program searches
.Ql "\&.wattle"
and
.Ql "zig-out/lib"
in the application directory,
and a vendored copy under
.Ql "deps"
is imported by a relative path.
Running the program needs
.Ic wattle
on the
.Ql "PATH"
and the prefix set with
.Ql "WATTLE_PREFIX" .
A program that needs neither is a
.Ql ":native"
exe.
Windows has no shebang lines,
so a
.Ql ":source"
exe cannot be installed there.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{:name \(dqgreeter\(dq
 :group \(dqnet\&.inqk\(dq
 :exes \(lB{:type :source
         :name \(dqgreet\(dq
         :entry \(dqmain\&.wattle\(dq
         :files \(lB\(dqmain\&.wattle\(dq \(dqlib\(dq \(dqdeps\(dq\(rB}\(rB
 :libs \(lB{:type :source
         :name \(dqutil\(dq
         :files \(lB\(dqutil/\(dq\(rB
         :for \(lB\(dqgreet\(dq\(rB}\(rB
 :docs \(lB{:type :man
         :files \(lB\(dqman/greet\&.1\(dq\(rB
         :for \(lB\(dqgreet\(dq\(rB}\(rB}
.Ed
.
.Ss Hooks
The application script defines a function for each hook it uses.
Each takes the application’s manifest.
The hooks run in this order at installation:
.Pp
.Bl -enum -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Ql "clean" ,
only when a clean build is requested
.It
.Ql "build"
.It
.Ql "install"
.It
.Ql "check" ,
only when a check is requested
.El
.Pp
The
.Ql "remove"
hook runs when the application is removed.
.Pp
Within a hook,
these functions add files to the manifest,
so that
.Ql "wattle apps remove"
can remove them:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql "app/add-bin"
.Xc
Adds a program to the binpath.
.It Xo
.Ql "app/add-manpage"
.Xc
Adds a man page to the manpath.
.El
.Pp
Example of
.Ql "hooks/init\&.wattle" :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\*(lpdefn install
  \(lBmanifest &\(rB
  \*(lpapp/add-bin manifest \(dqhello\(dq\*(rp
  \*(lpapp/add-manpage manifest \(dqhello\&.1\(dq\*(rp\*(rp
.Ed
.
.Sh INSTALLED FILES
All locations are under
.Ql "*prefix*" ;
see
.Ql "WATTLE_PREFIX"
in
.Xr wattle 1 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql "lib/wattle"
.Xc
The libpath,
which holds the applications.
.Ql "import"
does not search it.
See
.Ql "MODULES"
in
.Xr wattle 7 .
.It Xo
.Ql "lib/wattle/apps/<group>/<name>"
.Xc
The directory of an installed application:
.Ql "manifest\&.edn" ,
which lists its files and records its source,
.Ql ":rev" ,
the revision of the source,
and the revision of each remote lib,
a copy of its info file and a copy of its application script,
with the rest of its
.Ql "hooks"
directory.
The revision is the commit hash for a Git repository,
and
.Ql "sha256:"
and a hash of the files for a tarball or a directory.
.It Xo
.Ql "bin"
.Xc
The binpath,
for programs.
.It Xo
.Ql "share/man"
.Xc
The manpath,
for man pages.
.El
.
